version:    0.9.1 (the crate this project also depends on, to read Zstandard)
copied:     2026-11-14

What is here:
  Nothing but the licence. What came from the project lives in
  crates/shape-tools/src/zstd/:

  - bits.rs: src/bit_io/bit_writer.rs, the bit writer;
  - fse.rs: src/fse/fse_encoder.rs, the FSE tables (states from
    probabilities, a table's description, the two-state stream of
    Huffman weights, the three predefined distributions);
  - huff0.rs: src/huff0/huff0_encoder.rs, the Huffman codes from
    weights and the one- and four-stream writers.

  Each copied as it is, with its imports changed to this crate's and
  its tests and test-only functions left out (the crate keeps these
  modules private, so they cannot be used from it).

What was read:
  src/encoding/blocks/compressed.rs (how a compressed block is laid
  out: the literals section's header, the sequences' three codes and
  the order their bits are written in). crates/shape-tools/src/zstd/mod.rs
  follows that layout and RFC 8878; its matcher (hash chains, a look
  one byte ahead, repeated offsets), its code lengths and
  probabilities from counts, and its choice between a described, a
  predefined and a one-symbol table are this project's own
  (docs/research.md §77).
